From: FlaxAdvisors
Subject: appcommands: FRU-derived manufacturer/product IDs and Flax fw revision

Get Device ID previously reported Manufacturer 343 (Intel), Product 0, and
Firmware Revision 0.00 on TiogaPass.  Three fixes:

1. Manufacturer ID and Product ID now follow the board vendor.  The same image
   runs on Wiwynn and Quanta boards, so these must match the FRU.
   flax-ipmi-devid-manuf.service reads the FRU PRODUCT_MANUFACTURER from D-Bus
   at boot and caches the matching numeric IDs (decimal) in
   /var/cache/private/manufID and /var/cache/private/prodID; this handler reads
   them, keeping D-Bus out of the Get Device ID hot path.  dev_id.json supplies
   the fallback (Wiwynn) until the cache files appear.
     Wiwynn -> manuf 40092 (0x9C9C), product 7220  (0x1C34)
     Quanta -> manuf 40981 (0xA015), product 12614 (0x3146)
   The old /var/cache/private/prodID reader was hard-capped at 4 characters
   (std::string id = "0x00"), which truncated 0x1C34/0x3146; it is replaced.
   Product ID also gains a dev_id.json "prod_id" fallback.

2. Firmware Revision is now derived from the real BMC version.  The os-release
   string (e.g. "flax-onetree-1.0.7") carries a 3-part semantic version that
   never matched convertIntelVersion()'s git-style regexes, so the revision was
   always 0.00.  IPMI Get Device ID has only a 7-bit major field and an 8-bit
   BCD minor field, so all three components are packed:
     Firmware Revision major = ((X - 1) << 6) | Y
     Firmware Revision minor = BCD(Z)
   e.g. 1.0.7 -> 0x00 / 0x07 ; 2.1.8 -> 0x41 / 0x08.
   NOTE: (X-1) occupies the top two bits of the 7-bit major field, so major
   versions >= 3 overflow.  Revisit before shipping a 3.x firmware.

--- a/src/appcommands.cpp
+++ b/src/appcommands.cpp
@@ -291,6 +291,7 @@
